<main id="top">

  <div class="wrap hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Nevarro Technologies · Bengaluru, India</div>
    <h1>We build businesses toward <em>an outcome</em>.</h1>
    <p class="prose">Nevarro is a growth partner. We work inside companies to transform how they operate and scale them toward a strategic outcome — an acquisition, a listing, a next chapter. And we build the AI that makes it possible, through our own research and development.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn primary" href="mailto:adi@nevarrotech.com?subject=Enquiry">Talk to us</a>
      <a class="btn secondary" href="#tracks">Our two tracks →</a>
    </div>

    <div class="panel">
      <div class="bar"><i></i><i></i><i></i><em>nevarro — studio</em></div>
      <div class="stage">
        <div class="globe-wrap" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg id="globeSvg" viewBox="0 0 600 400">
            <g id="gRingBack" transform="rotate(-16 300 200)"></g>
            <g id="gGlobe"></g>
            <g id="gRingFront" transform="rotate(-16 300 200)"></g>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="caption">Partners in the business. Builders of the technology.</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="strip">
    <div class="inner">
      <span>Growth partnership</span>
      <span>Applied AI research</span>
      <span>Strategic outcomes</span>
      <span>Bengaluru, India</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- TWO TRACKS -->
  <section id="tracks"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow rev">The thesis</div>
    <h2 class="rev">Two tracks.</h2>
    <p class="prose rev">Advisors hand over a deck and leave. Vendors ship a product and invoice. We do neither — we take a position in the outcome, and we build what the business needs to get there.</p>
    <div class="tracks">
      <div class="track rev">
        <div class="tnum">Track one</div>
        <h3>Growth partnership</h3>
        <p>We work with a small number of companies at a time, inside the business rather than beside it. We rebuild how the operation runs, put technology where the manual work is, and grow toward a defined target. The engagement is written around that target — and the destination is a strategic outcome: an acquisition, a listing, or a transition into whatever comes next.</p>
        <div class="tlist">Transformation · Scale · Strategic exit</div>
      </div>
      <div class="track rev">
        <div class="tnum">Track two</div>
        <h3>Applied AI research</h3>
        <p>Our internal research and development team builds custom AI products and models for industries the large platforms overlook. Each one starts from a real operating problem, is trained on the language and constraints of that sector, and becomes part of the stack we bring into the next partnership.</p>
        <div class="tlist">Research · Custom models · Industry products</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <!-- HOW WE PARTNER -->
  <section id="approach"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow rev">How we partner</div>
    <h2 class="rev">Aligned to the outcome, not the invoice.</h2>
    <p class="prose rev">We take on few engagements because each one is deep. The shape is consistent even when the terms are not.</p>
    <div class="lines">
      <div class="line rev">
        <div class="k">We go inside</div>
        <p>We work within the operation, alongside the people who run it. Nothing useful gets built from the outside looking in.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="line rev">
        <div class="k">We target growth</div>
        <p>Every engagement is written around a defined target rather than a scope of hours. What we are aiming at is agreed at the start, in writing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="line rev">
        <div class="k">We build, not advise</div>
        <p>Technology replaces the manual work rather than documenting it. What we build stays with the business.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="line rev">
        <div class="k">We aim at an outcome</div>
        <p>The destination is a strategic event — an acquisition, a listing, a transition — and the work is structured to arrive there.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="line rev">
        <div class="k">Custom terms</div>
        <p>Every partnership is structured to the situation and agreed in writing before it begins. There is no standard package, because there is no standard company.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <!-- FOCUS -->
  <section id="focus"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow rev">Where we focus</div>
    <h2 class="rev">Niche industries, deep operations.</h2>
    <p class="prose rev">We look for sectors with real operational depth, meaningful regulation, and software that has not kept pace — where a small team working closely with an operator can change the trajectory of the business.</p>
    <div class="lines">
      <div class="line rev">
        <div class="k">Healthcare</div>
        <p>Providers and practices where operations, compliance, and patient-facing systems have grown faster than the tooling around them.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="line rev">
        <div class="k">Financial services</div>
        <p>Advisers, intermediaries, and regulated entities carrying heavy documentation and reporting obligations.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="line rev">
        <div class="k">ITSM</div>
        <p>Service management operations where volume is high, process is well defined, and the work remains stubbornly manual.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="line rev">
        <div class="k">Information management</div>
        <p>Businesses whose core asset is documents and records, and whose competitive edge is how quickly they can be found and used.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="line rev">
        <div class="k">Outsourcing</div>
        <p>Delivery organisations built on people, where AI shifts the economics of every process it touches.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  <section class="closing"><div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow rev">Ready when you are</div>
    <h2 class="rev">If you're building toward something, let's talk.</h2>
    <p class="prose rev">Whether you are scaling toward an exit or trying to work out what the next chapter looks like, a short email is enough to start.</p>
    <div class="cta-row rev">
      <a class="btn primary" href="mailto:adi@nevarrotech.com?subject=Enquiry">Email us</a>
      <a class="btn secondary" href="/support">Visit support</a>
    </div>
  </div></section>

</main>

